## Decisions

:::decision{#D1 status=accepted date=2026-10-02 owner=@maya} Merge offline edits with CRDTs, not last-write-wins
Two people editing the same day offline must both keep their changes. Last-write-wins lost an edit in 1 of 9 test sessions.
:::

:::decision{#D2 status=proposed owner=@maya} One payment provider for the US and the EU
It keeps the PCI scope small. The provider must support SEPA transfers.
:::

:::question Launch payments in the EU at GA, or after?
@maya decides with legal by 2027-01-15. Until then, plan for the US only.
:::

## Risks

:::risk{impact=high likelihood=medium owner=@ops status=open} The PCI review takes longer than eight weeks
Start in January with the provider's pre-certified checkout, and keep a hosted checkout page as the fallback.
:::

:::risk{impact=critical likelihood=low owner=@maya status=open} The provider drops SEPA support
D2 would fail in the EU. Keep a second provider's quote current until GA.
:::

:::risk{impact=medium likelihood=high owner=@li status=mitigated} Merged edits confuse people
An activity feed now shows who changed what, and testers stopped reporting lost plans.
:::

:::risk-matrix Roadmap risks
:::

